# um-texts 1
=== tip 10100
Open/Close Information window.

=== tip 10101
General view 
Show character's general 
view in the Information window.

=== tip 10102
Hit Locations
Show damage suffered by the 
character in the Information window.

=== tip 10103
Attributes
Show character's attributes 
in  the Information window.

=== tip 10104
Spell effects
Show spells cast on the character 
in the Information window.

=== tip 10200
Open/Close Text window.

=== tip 10201
Messages
Show messages 
in Text window.

=== tip 10202
Collected items
Show details on collected 
items in the Text window.

=== tip 10300
Open/Close Mini-map

=== tip 10301
Zoom in 
Increase Mini-map's scale.

=== tip 10302
Zoom out 
Decrease Mini-map's scale.

=== tip 10303
Default camera view
Turn camera North.

=== tip 10400
Pause On/Off
When pause is on, you can give orders 
to characters, change their weapons, and 
assign targets.

=== tip 10401
Call up Quests screen
Shows completed and available 
quests and objectives.

=== tip 10402
Normal speed
Set game speed to normal.

=== tip 10403
Accelerated speed
Set game speed to high.

=== tip 10500
Aggressive/Defensive mode
In "Aggressive" mode the character 
will attack all enemies who see him. 
In "Defensive" mode he will only attack 
after you've issued the command.

=== tip 10501
Crawl
When a character crawls, he makes 
much less noise than when he walks 
and he is much less visible to enemies.
His speed is very low. "Stamina" will 
neither diminish nor increase.

=== tip 10502
Sneak
When sneaking, characters make almost no 
sound and enemies have a very tough time detecting 
them. Speed is low. "Stamina" will neither 
diminish nor increase.

=== tip 10503
Walk
When a character walks, his speed is 
normal. "Stamina" will neither diminish 
nor increase.

=== tip 10504
Run
When a character runs, he makes more noise than when 
he walks, so he attracts the attention of enemies who 
otherwise couldn't see him. Speed is high. "Stamina" diminishes; 
when it reaches zero, the character will automatically start 
walking.

=== tip 10510
Follow
Follow a short distance behind 
the selected character.

=== tip 10511
Steal something from character/Use an item
If you place the mask-shaped cursor over a live character 
and click, you can steal things from him (provided he has anything 
to steal).If you place the hand-shaped cursor over an item and 
click, you can use that item (if that's possible).

=== tip 20100
Equip character
This screen allows you to distribute 
weapons and armor among 
your characters.

=== tip 20101
Skills/Spells
This screen allows you to distribute spells among 
characters and to acquire new skills or improve 
existing ones.

=== tip 20102
Item shop 
This screen allows you to buy and sell items 
and components (blueprints and materials).

=== tip 20103
Item constructor 
This screen allows you to construct new 
items and deconstruct existing ones.

=== tip 20104
Repair Items
This screen allows you to repair items which 
have become less reliable through wear-and-tear.

=== tip 20105
Spell shop 
This screen allows you to buy and sell spells 
and components (keystones and runes).

=== tip 20106
Spell constructor
This mode allows you to construct new 
spells and deconstruct existing ones.

=== tip 20107
Exit
Exit from camp or shop.

=== tip 20200
Accept
Confirm all changes you've made in this screen.

=== tip 20201
Cancel
Cancel all actions you've made in this screen.
If you leave camp or shop without confirming 
your changes, they'll be cancelled automatically.

=== tip 20300
Previous character
Shows the previous character in the Hero's party.

=== tip 20301
Next character
Shows next character in the Hero's party.

=== tip 20302
Dismiss character
The selected character will leave your party.
He will return to his former location and 
you will be able to recruit him again later.

=== tip 20303
Heal wounds 
Completely heals all damage suffered 
by the character. Crippled limbs which cannot 
be repaired by an ordinary healing spell will also be healed.

=== tip 20400
Scroll
Available items and spells - scroll to the right. 
If you press the <SHIFT> key, the list will scroll to 
the last item.

=== tip 20401
Scroll
Available items and spells - scroll to the left. 
If you press the <SHIFT> key, the list will scroll to 
the first item.

=== tip 20500
Yes

=== tip 20501
Cancel

=== tip 21000
Blueprints: weapons
Shows blueprints for making 
weapons.
Note: Characters cannot equip
blueprints. They can only be used
in the Items constructor.

=== tip 21001
Blueprints: light armor
Shows blueprints for making 
light armor.
Note: characters cannot equip
blueprints. They can only
be used in the Items constructor.

=== tip 21002
Blueprints: Heavy armor
Shows blueprints for making heavy armor.

=== tip 21003
Potions and wands
Shows ready-made potions, wands and unique 
magical items as well as the blueprints to make them.

=== tip 21004
Materials
Shows materials needed to 
make different items.

=== tip 21005
Ready-made items 
Shows only items ready for use.

=== tip 21100
Blueprints and materials
Shows only materials and blueprints
for making items.
Note: characters cannot equip
or wear blueprints or materials.
You can only use these items
in the Items constructor.

=== tip 21101
Keystones and runes
Shows only keystones 
and runes.
Note: characters cannot equip
keystones or runes. You
can only use these items in
the Spells constructor.

=== tip 21102
Ready-made items and spells
Shows only items and spells ready for use.

=== tip 21103
Collected items
Shows collected items only. These items can
not be used, but can be sold for money.

=== tip 21104
Quest items 
Shows only quest items necessary
for completing quests.

=== tip 21105
All items you have
Shows all items you currently have.

=== tip 21200
Keystones: Elemental Magic 
Shows keystones for making spells of 
the Magic of Elements school.
Note: characters cannot equip
keystones. They can only be used
in the Spells constructor.

=== tip 21201
Keystones: Sensory Magic
Shows keystones for making spells of 
the Sensory Magic school.
Note: characters cannot equip
keystones. They can only be used
in the Spells constructor.

=== tip 21202
Keystones: Astral Magic
Shows keystones for making spells of 
the Astral Magic school.
Note: characters cannot equip
keystones. They can only be used
in the Spells constructor.

=== tip 21203
Rune: Basic
Shows runes which allow you to improve 
spell properties.
Note: Characters cannot equip
runes. They can only be used
in Spells constructor.

=== tip 21204
Runes: Special
Shows runes which allow you to limit the range 
of a spell and insert the spell into weapons or armor.
Note: characters cannot equip runes. They can 
only be used in the Spell constructor.

=== tip 21205
Ready-made spells 
Shows spells which are ready for use.

=== tip 30100
Close
Removes tips from screen.

=== tip 30101
Previous screen
Shows previous tips screen.

=== tip 30102
Next screen
Shows next tips screen.

=== tip 30103
Exit to Windows

