=== tip 80100
Go to Game Zone

=== tip 80101
Return to Global map

=== tip 80102
Return to Game zone

=== tip 80110
Entrances to Game zone
Available entrances are marked in green, 
unavailable in red. To choose an entrance, 
click on it.

=== tip 80111
Quests
Completed quests are marked with "V",
failed quests or those which are impossible 
to complete are marked with "X".
Unmarked quests are currently incomplete. 
To get a description on a quest, click on it.

=== tip 80112
Quest area
The cross on the map shows 
the approximate location of the 
selected quest.
Note: In certain quests the targets 
can move around the Game zone or 
can be located in different places. 
In such a case the cross is an 
approximation.

=== tip 80200
Previous zone.
Shows previous Game zone
with all uncompleted quests.

=== tip 80201
Next zone
Shows the next Game zone
with all uncompleted quests.

=== tip 90100
Go to "Camp"
Here you can give your characters
new clothes, weapons and spend experience
points gained during the quests.

=== tip 90101
Turn map left

=== tip 90102
Turn map right

=== tip action_accel
Accelerated game speed.
The time will accelerate. 
Characters and enemies 
will move and attack faster.

=== tip action_camera1
Camera 1
When you press this key + <CTRL> key, all camera settings 
will be saved as "Settings 1". If you press the key again 
without the <CTRL> key, the camera will immediately return to the 
Settings 1 position.

=== tip action_camera2
Camera 2
When you press this key + <CTRL> key, camera settings 
will be saved as "Settings 2". If you press this key again 
without the <CTRL> key, the camera will immediately return to the 
Settings 2 position.

=== tip action_camera3
Camera 3
When you press this key + <CTRL> key, camera settings 
will be saved as "Settings 3". If you press this key again 
without the <CTRL> key, the camera will immediately return to the 
Settings 3 position.

=== tip action_camera4
Camera 4
When you press this key + <CTRL> key, camera settings 
will be saved as "Settings 4". If you press this key again 
without the <CTRL> key, the camera will immediately return to the 
Settings 4 position.

=== tip action_camera_center
Point camera
Point camera at the selected character.

=== tip action_camera_down
Camera back
Camera scrolls back. If you press this key + <CTRL>, 
the camera will move back, but remain pointed in the same direction.

=== tip action_camera_left
Camera left
Camera scrolls left. If you press this key + <CTRL>, 
the camera will move left, but remain pointed in the same direction.

=== tip action_camera_norm
Camera north
Return camera to pointing North.

=== tip action_camera_right
Camera right
Camera scrolls right. If you press this key + <CTRL>, 
the camera will move right while remaining in the same direction.

=== tip action_camera_track
Tracking
Camera will track the selected character. 
You can also set the angle, focus and zoom features.

=== tip action_camera_up
Camera forward
Camera scrolls forward. If you press this key + <CTRL>, 
camera will move forward while focusing in the same direction.

=== tip action_camera_zoom_in
Zoom in
Camera zooms in on the selected target.

=== tip action_camera_zoom_out
Zoom out
Camera zooms out from the selected target.

=== tip action_cancel_target
Cancel action
To perform certain actions (such as cast a spell, steal, use) 
you must select the appropriate icon first and then 
place the cursor on the target. The button you assign 
now allows you to bypass the icon selection. You can also 
use the <ESC> key to cancel any action.

=== tip action_crawl
Crawl
When a character crawls, he makes much less noise 
than when he walks and he is much less visible to 
enemies. His speed is very low. "Stamina" will neither 
diminish nor increase.

=== tip action_cs_body
Aim at body
Your character will aim at the enemy's body 
when attacking. When the body's "health" 
reaches 0, the enemy will die.

=== tip action_cs_head
Aim at head
Your character will aim at the enemy's head 
when attacking. When the head's "health" 
reaches 0, the enemy will die.

=== tip action_cs_lhand
Aim at left hand
Your character will aim at the enemy's left hand 
when attacking. When the hand's "health" reaches 0, 
the enemy will fight and cast spells much slower.

=== tip action_cs_lleg
Aim at left leg
Your character will aim at the enemy's left leg when 
attacking. When the leg's "health" reaches 0, the enemy 
will move much slower.

=== tip action_cs_rhand
Aim at right hand
Your character will aim at the enemy's right hand when 
attacking. When the hand's "health" reaches 0, the enemy 
will fight and cast spells much slower.

=== tip action_cs_rleg
Aim at right leg
Your character will aim at the enemy's right leg when 
attacking. When the leg's "health" reaches 0, the enemy 
will move much slower.

=== tip action_decel
Normal game speed
The time will pass normally.

=== tip action_follow
Follow
Selected character will follow the designated 
character until you give him another command.

=== tip action_item1
Potion or wand 1
Use the first potion or wand (item
icons are counted from right to left).

=== tip action_item2
Potion or wand 2
Use the second potion or wand (item 
icons are counted from right to left).

=== tip action_item3
Potion or wand 3
Use the third potion or wand (item 
icons are counted from right to left).

=== tip action_item4
Potion or wand 4
Use the fourth potion or wand (item 
icons are counted from right to left).

=== tip action_obj
Quests screen
This screen provides details on 
available quests and their status.

=== tip action_pause
Pause mode
When the game is paused, you can control 
the camera and give orders to your characters.
Orders will be carried out when the game is
unpaused.

=== tip action_quickload
Quick load
Load the game saved as "Quick Save" 
without switching to the Esc-menu.

=== tip action_quicksave
Quick save
The game will be saved without switching
to the Esc-menu under the default name "Quick Save".

=== tip action_run
Run
When a character runs, he makes more noise than 
when he walks, thereby attracting the attention of 
enemies who otherwise would not see him. 
Speed is high. 
"Stamina" diminishes; when it reaches zero,
the character will automatically start walking.

=== tip action_select1
Select character 1
This will select your first character (character 
icons are counted from left to right).

=== tip action_select2
Select character 2
This will select your second character (character 
icons are counted from left to right).

=== tip action_select3
Select character 3
This will select your third character (character 
icons are counted from left to right).

=== tip action_select_all
Select all
This will select all your characters.

=== tip action_sneak
Sneak
When sneaking around, characters make almost no 
sound. Speed is low. "Stamina" will neither 
diminish nor increase.

=== tip action_spell1
Spell 1
Cast the first available spell (Spell 
icons are counted from top to bottom).

=== tip action_spell2
Spell 2
Cast the second available spell (Spell 
icons are counted from top to bottom).

=== tip action_spell3
Spell 3
Cast the third available spell (Spell 
icons are counted from top to bottom).

=== tip action_spell4
Spell 4
Cast the fourth available spell (Spell 
icons are counted from top to bottom).

=== tip action_spell5
Spell 5
Cast the fifth available spell (Spell 
icons are counted from top to bottom).

=== tip action_spell6
Spell 6
Cast the sixth available spell (Spell 
icons are counted from top to bottom).

=== tip action_spell7
Spell 7
Cast the seventh available spell (Spell 
icons are counted from top to bottom).

=== tip action_spell8
Spell 8
Cast the eighth available spell (Spell 
icons are counted from top to bottom).

=== tip action_swarm
Aggressive/Defensive mode
This switches a character's mode between "aggressive" and "defensive".
In "Aggressive" mode the character will attack all enemies who have detected him. 
In "Defensive" mode he will only attack after you issue the appropriate 
command.

=== tip action_tutorial_script
Tutorial
This key will call up a tutorial for 
the current training quest or
interface screen.

=== tip action_use_science
Use/Steal
You can use mechanical items (open locks, turn 
switches etc.) You can also steal something 
directly from live enemies. Your success rate 
will depend on your "Use/Steal" skill.

=== tip action_w_info1
General view
The Information window will show a general view of the 
character you've placed the cursor on. If the cursor is 
not placed on anyone, the Information window will 
show the currently selected character.

=== tip action_w_info2
Hit locations
The Information window will show damage to the body 
parts of the character you've placed the cursor on. 
If the cursor is not placed on anyone, the Information 
window will show the currently selected character.

=== tip action_w_info3
Attributes
The Information window will show details on the 
character you've placed the cursor on. If the cursor 
is not placed on anyone, the Information window 
will show the currently selected character.

=== tip action_w_info4
Spell effects
The Information window will show the spells currently affecting the 
character you've placed the cursor on. If the cursor is not
placed on anyone, the Information window will show the 
currently selected character.

=== tip action_w_minimap
Show/Hide Mini-map.

=== tip action_w_text1
Messages
The Text window will show messages generated 
during the game (completion of objectives, sub-titles,
messages about collected items etc.).

=== tip action_w_text2
Collected items
The Text window will show a list of all items 
picked up by the character in the current Game zone.

=== tip action_walk
Walk
When a character walks, his speed is normal. 
"Stamina" neither diminishes nor increases.

=== tip action_weapon1
Weapon 1
Select the first available weapon (weapon 
icons are counted from left to right).

=== tip action_weapon2
Weapon 2
Select the second available weapon (weapon 
icons are counted from left to right).

=== tip action_weapon3
Weapon 3
Select the third available weapon (weapon 
icons are counted from left to right).

=== tip action_weapon4
Weapon 4
Select the fourth available weapon (weapon 
icons are counted from left to right).

=== tip option_autosave
Autosave
On: autosave will be performed 
each time you enter or exit a 
Game zone or a Dialog zone.
Off: no autosave.

=== tip option_brightness
Brightness
Adjust the brightness of game images.

=== tip option_camera_reverse_x
Inverse camera left/right rotation
When rotating the camera left/right with the 
right mouse button pressed, the direction 
of the camera rotation may be changed:  
Off: The camera will rotate accodingly to 
the direction of the mouse shifted left or 
right.
On: The camera will rotate in the direction 
opposite to that where mouse moves.

=== tip option_camera_reverse_y
Inverse camera up/down move
When moving the camera up/down with the 
right mouse button pressed, the direction of 
the camera movement may be changed:
Off: The camera will turn accordingly to 
the direction of the mouse shifted up or down.
On: The camera will turn in the direction 
opposite to that where mouse moves.

=== tip option_contrast
Contrast
Adjust the contrast of game images.

=== tip option_difficulty
Difficulty level

Novice
Familiarization mode: enemies weaker, stealth and strategy 
requirements reduced.

Normal
Requires high degree of stealth and strategy. Enemy 
capabilities fully enabled.

Note: You can change difficulty level at any moment during 
the game using game options menu.

=== tip option_footprints
Show footprints
On: show footprints. Off: do not show footprints.

=== tip option_gamma
Gamma-correction
Adjust the gamma-correction of game images.

=== tip option_group_actions
Command options
Set options for controlling your characters.

=== tip option_group_camera
Camera management options
Set options for managing the camera
("free" mode or fixed settings).

=== tip option_group_cshots
Combat options
Set options for assigning hot keys 
for precision blows.

=== tip option_group_game
Game options
Set general game options.

=== tip option_group_items
Item options
Set options for using game items.

=== tip option_group_select
Character selection options
Set options for selecting characters.

=== tip option_group_sens
Sensitivity options
Set keyboard and mouse sensitivity.

=== tip option_group_sound
Sound options
Set options for sound management: 
volume of music, speech, sound effects.

=== tip option_group_spells
Magic options
Set options for using spells.

=== tip option_group_video
Graphics options
Set the game's graphic options.

=== tip option_group_windows
Screen management options
Set options for game windows.

=== tip option_marks
Show blood
On: after a character dies, a puddle 
of blood will appear on the ground. 
Off: will not show blood.

=== tip option_power_kbd
Keyboard sensitivity
Adjust the camera's speed when 
controlled by the keyboard.

=== tip option_power_mouse
Mouse sensitivity
Adjust cursor speed, camera rotation speed 
and other actions controlled by the mouse.

=== tip option_reverse_stereo
Reverse the right and 
the left sound channels
On: reverse channels (change the 
left and the right ones). 
Off: Default sound channels 
settings

=== tip option_rubber_select
Frame selection
Sets the distance you need to move the mouse in order 
to begin frame selection. Left position disables frame
selection.

=== tip option_scroll_border
Scrolling border
Sets the distance between the cursor and 
the screen border to start scrolling the camera from. 
The camera scrolls in the direction the cursor moves.

=== tip option_select_type
Character selection
On: the selected character will be shown with a special 
marker (triangle) and highlighted. 
Off: no markers will be shown (selected characters will 
only be highlighted).

=== tip option_shadow_buildings
Object shadows
If your system barely exceeds the minimum requirements, 
we recommend that you turn object shadows 
(buildings, bridges etc.) off.

=== tip option_shadow_flora
Tree shadows
If your system barely exceeds the minimum 
requirements, we recommend that you turn 
tree shadows off.

=== tip option_shadow_other
All shadows
If your system barely exceeds the minimum requirements, 
we recommend that you turn off shadows from additional 
light sources. If you turn off all shadows, other 
shadow controls will no longer apply.

=== tip option_shadow_units
Character shadows
If your system barely exceeds minimum requirements, 
we recommend that you turn character shadows off.

=== tip option_show_flying_hp
Show hit results
You can see the result of every blow in the game: damage inflicted 
by the characters, method of damage infliction, and experience gained. 
These results can be seen as strings and numbers flying away 
from the character after hit.
On: show hit results. 
Off: do not show hit results.

=== tip option_show_path
Show path
On: show the character's path to the selected destination. 
Off: do not show path.

=== tip option_show_tutorial
Tutorial screens
To help you master the game 
quickly we have provided 
a number of tutorial screens.
On: show tutorial screens.
Off: do not show tutorial screens.

=== tip option_switch_filters
Autofilters
You can use inventory filters to display only 
those items belonging to a particular category. 
These filers may be activated only manually 
or both manually and automatically.
On: the filters will be switched on automatically 
every time a new item is put into inventory 
(according to the item type).
Off: the filers will be switched on/off only 
manually.

=== tip option_tooltip_time
Tips delay
This option sets the delay time for 
of the tips popping up near the screen 
element you placed the cursor over.
The range is between 0 and 5 seconds.

=== tip option_volume_sfx
Sound volume
Sets the volume of sound effects.

=== tip option_volume_stream
Music volume
Sets the music volume.

=== tip option_volume_voice
Speech volume
Sets the voices volume.

